    "excerpt": "VBOC-2024-01 Funder/Agency: U.S. Small Business Administration (SBA) Opportunity Number: SB-OVVB-24-001 Description: The purpose of this Funding Opportunity is to invite proposals to provide quality t...",
    "bodyText": "\nSearch\n\nOpportunity Title:\n\nVBOC-2024-01\n\n \n\nFunder/Agency:\n\nU.S. Small Business Administration (SBA)\n\n \n\nOpportunity Number:\n\nSB-OVVB-24-001\n\n \n\nDescription:\n\nThe purpose of this Funding Opportunity is to invite proposals to provide quality training and counseling to veteran small business owners and entrepreneurs. A key component of this Funding Opportunity is for applicants to provide training to transitioning military personnel and spouses through the Boots to Business (B2B) Training Program, and to veterans and military spouses through the Reboot and Military Spouse Pathway to Business Training Programs.\n\n\n\n\nAdditionally, applicants will provide counseling, training, technical and financial skill development, comprehensive business assessments and mentoring services to veteran, active duty, Reserve, National Guard, military spouse and family member entrepreneurs, and small business owners interested in starting, expanding and diversifying small businesses.\n\n\n\n\nGrant Announcement Q&A Sessions\n\n\n\n\nOVBD will host conference calls on the following dates/times to provide additional information and address questions related to this funding opportunity.\n\nJune 27, 2024: 4pm ET\n\nJuly 12, 2024: 3pm ET\n\n\n\n\nClick here to join the meeting\n\nMeeting ID: 244 647 200 565\n\nPasscode: U7xYbE\n\n\n\n\nOr call in (audio only)\n\n+1 202-765-1264, 265542768# Phone Conference ID: 736 752 338#\n\n \n\nEligibility:\n\nNonprofits\n\nLocal and state government agencies\n\nPrivate sector firms\n\nInstitutions of higher education\n\n \n\nAward Details:\n\nTotal Amount Available:\n\n$1,100,000\n\n \n\nMaximum Award:\n\n$400,000\n\n \n\nMinimum Award:\n\n$340,000\n\n \n\nDeadline:\n\nApplications Due July 19, 2024\n\n \n\nOpportunity Link\n\n \n\nGrant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation.\n\nOpportunity Title: Mine Health and Safety State Grants Funder/Agency: Department of Labor (DOL), Mine Safety and Health Administration...\n\nOpportunity Title: CalCompetes Fiscal Year 2024-25 Notice Announcement Funder/Agency: California Governor's Office of Business and...\n\nOpportunity Title: YouthBuild Funder/Agency: DOL Opportunity Number: FOA-ETA-24-53 Description: Under this Funding Opportunity...\n\n",
