    "slug": "coming-soon-dol-youthbuild-grants-for-education-and-training-anticipated-release-mid-july",
    "title": "Coming Soon: DOL YouthBuild Grants for Education and Training – Anticipated Release Mid-July",
    "excerpt": "YouthBuild Funder/Agency: DOL Opportunity Number: FOA-ETA-24-53 Description: Under this Funding Opportunity Announcement (FOA), DOL will award grants through a competitive process to organizations pro...",
    "bodyText": "\n\nSearch\n\nOpportunity Title:\n\nYouthBuild\n\n\n\n\nFunder/Agency:\n\nDOL\n\n\n\n\nOpportunity Number:\n\nFOA-ETA-24-53\n\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\nUnder this Funding Opportunity Announcement (FOA), DOL will award grants through a competitive process to organizations providing pre-apprenticeship services that support education, occupational skills training, and employment services to opportunity youth, ages 16 to 24, who are performing meaningful work and service to their communities.\n\n\n\n\nThe YouthBuild program model prepares participants for quality jobs in a variety of careers, in diverse industry sectors, particularly in infrastructure sectors, and includes wrap-around services such as mentoring, trauma-informed care, personal counseling, transportation supports, and employment preparation - all key strategies for addressing violence in communities. Applicants must include construction skills training and may include occupational skills training in other in-demand industries. This expansion into additional in-demand industries is the Construction Plus component.\n\n\n\n\nEligibility:\n\nPublic, State, or Private controlled institutions of higher education\n\nNative American tribal governments and organizations\n\nNonprofits\n\nCity, township, or county governments\n\nIndependent school districts\n\nState governments\n\nSpecial district governments\n\nPublic housing authorities/Indian housing authorities\n\n\n\n\n\nAward Details:\n\nTotal Amount Available:\n\n$99,000,000\n\n\n\n\nMaximum Award:\n\n$1,500,000\n\n\n\n\nMinimum Award:\n\n$700,000\n\n\n\n\nDeadline:\n\nAnticipated Release: July 15, 2024\n\nAnticipated Deadline: September 16, 2024\n\n\n\n\nOpportunity Link\n\n\n\n\nGrant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation.\n\nOpportunity Title: California Education Learning Lab's AI Challenge Funder/Agency: Governor's Office of Planning and Research (OPR)...\n\nOpportunity Title: ROSS (Resident Opportunity and Self-Sufficiency) Service Coordinator Program - FY2024 - NOFO Funder/Agency: Department...\n\nOpportunity Title: Mine Health and Safety State Grants Funder/Agency: Department of Labor (DOL), Mine Safety and Health Administration...\n\n",
