    "slug": "hud-preservation-and-reinvestment-initiative-for-community-enhancement-price-due-07-10-24",
    "title": "HUD Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) - Due 07/10/24",
    "excerpt": "Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) Competition Funder/Agency: Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) Opportunity Number: FR-6700-N-99 Description: HU...",
    "bodyText": "\nSearch\n\nOpportunity Title:\n\nPreservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) Competition\n\n\n\n\nFunder/Agency:\n\nDepartment of Housing and Urban Development (HUD)\n\n\n\n\nOpportunity Number:\n\nFR-6700-N-99\n\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\nHUD has issued a Notice of Funding Opportunity (NOFO) which appropriates $235 million in competitive grant funding for the preservation and revitalization of manufactured housing and eligible manufactured housing communities. Congress has directed HUD to undertake this competition using the Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) statutory and regulatory framework for this first-of-its-kind initiative. PRICE supports communities in their efforts to maintain, protect, and stabilize manufactured housing and Manufactured Housing Communities (MHCs). Of the $235 million available in PRICE funding, $210 million is reserved for the main PRICE competition (PRICE Main). HCD is requesting the maximum award of $75 million under the PRICE Main competition.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCalifornia-Specific Information:\n\nThe California Department of Housing and Community Development (HCD) is soliciting public review and comment on its application for the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) grant competition.\n\n\n\n\nPlease submit your written comments to PRICE@hcd.ca.gov.\n\n\n\n\nMailed comments will also be accepted if postmarked no later than\n\nJune 14, 2024.\n\n\n\n\nComments may be mailed to:\n\nDepartment of Housing and Community Development\n\n2020 W. El Camino Ave\n\nSacramento CA, 95833\n\nFederal Branch Suite 200\n\nAttention: Brad Satterwhite, PRICE Coordinator\n\n \n\nEligibility:\n\nState and local governmental entities\n\nMultijurisdictional Entities\n\nMetropolitan Planning Organizations (MPO)\n\nResident-controlled MHCs\n\nCooperatives\n\nNon-profit entities (including consortia of non-profit entities)\n\nCDFIs\n\nIndian Tribes or their Tribally Designated Housing Entities (TDHEs), Tribal non-profits and Native CDFIs\n\n \n\nAward Details:\n\nTotal Amount Available:\n\n$235,000,000\n\n \n\nDeadline:\n\nApplications Due July 10, 2024\n\n \n\nOpportunity Link\n\n \n\nGrant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation.\n\nOpportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement...\n\nOpportunity Title: ROSS (Resident Opportunity and Self-Sufficiency) Service Coordinator Program - FY2024 - NOFO Funder/Agency: Department...\n\nOpportunity Title: Broadband Technical Assistance (BTA) Funder/Agency: Department of Agriculture (USDA), Rural Utilities Service (RUS)...\n\n",
