    "bodyText": "\nSearch\n\nOpportunity Title:\n\nPhysical and Digital Infrastructure Security Grant (DF) Program For Health Care Facilities\n\n\n\n\nFunder/Agency:\n\nGovernor's Office of Emergency Services\n\n\n\n\nOpportunity Number:\n\n60510\n\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\nThe purpose of the DF Program is to provide funding for physical facility and digital security enhancements to health care facilities providing abortion-related services and reproductive health care services throughout California that may be the target of violence and vandalism.\n\n\n\n\nEligibility:\n\nTo be eligible, Applicants must:\n\n1) be a currently licensed community health center, tribal health program, a non-profit hospital that is not part of a large health system or hospital system; or a nonprofit organization whose membership consists of the above licensed facilities;\n\n2) be located in California; and\n\n3) provide abortion-related services (or referrals to abortion-related services) and reproductive health care services.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAward Details:\n\n\n\n\nTotal Amount Available:\n\n$7,798,822\n\n\n\n\nMaximum Award:\n\n$750,000\n\n\n\n\nMinimum Award:\n\n$1\n\n\n\n\nDeadline:\n\nJune 6, 2024\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOpportunity Link\n\n\n\n\nGrant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation.\n\n\n\n\nOpportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement...\n\nOpportunity Title: NINDS Renewal Awards of SBIR Phase II Grants (Phase IIB) for Clinical Trials and Clinical Research (R44 Clinical Trial...\n\nOpportunity Title: Draft Module Announcement; Universal Patching and Remediation for Autonomous Defense (UPGRADE) Funder/Agency:...\n\n",
