    "slug": "hhs-small-business-transition-grant-for-new-entrepreneurs-applications-ongoing-until-04-05-27",
    "title": "HHS Small Business Transition Grant for New Entrepreneurs - Applications Ongoing Until 04/05/27",
    "excerpt": "Small Business Transition Grant for New Entrepreneurs (R43/R44 Clinical Trial Required) Funder/Agency: Department of Health and Human Services (HHS), National Institutes of Health (NIH) Opportunity Nu...",
    "bodyText": "\n\nSearch\n\nOpportunity Title:\n\nSmall Business Transition Grant for New Entrepreneurs (R43/R44 Clinical Trial Required)\n\n \n\nFunder/Agency:\n\nDepartment of Health and Human Services (HHS), National Institutes of Health (NIH)\n\n \n\nOpportunity Number:\n\nPAR-24-132\n\n \n\nDescription:\n\nThrough this Notice of Funding Opportunity (NOFO), the National Institutes of Health (NIH) aims to facilitate the career development and transition of investigators new to entrepreneurship with an interest in small business by simultaneously supporting their entrepreneurial development and the conduct of research and development under their direction.\n\n\n\n\nThis NOFO supports small business concerns (SBCs) in employing and developing researchers as entrepreneurial Program Directors/Principal Investigators (PDs/PIs). In addition to augmenting scientific research staff and supporting research and development efforts at SBCs, a major component of this NOFO is entrepreneurial training, mentoring, and career development of the PD/PI. Optimal PDs/PIs for this award are scientists and professionals with strong research, technology development, and/or healthcare delivery skills and experience, but limited entrepreneurial and independent research project leadership experience. PDs/PIs are expected to grow their entrepreneurial skillset while working in a small business to develop promising technologies and products that align with NIH's mission to improve health and save lives.\n\n\n\n\nPre-Application Webinar\n\n\n\n\nNIH will hold a technical assistance webinar on June 11th, 2024 from 3:00 PM to 5:00 PM (Eastern Time)\n\n\n\n\nWebinar Registration Link\n\n\n\n\nThe purpose of this webinar is to discuss the goals and objectives of the awarding components on the NOFO, highlight unique components of the application content and review criteria, and answer questions from attendees. Potential applicants are encouraged to submit their questions to NIH SEED (Small business Education and Entrepreneurial Development) at SEEDinfo@nih.gov in advance of the webinar.\n\n \n\nEligibility:\n\nSmall businesses\n\n \n\nDeadline:\n\nApplications Ongoing Until April 05, 2027\n\n \n\nOpportunity Link\n\n \n\nGrant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation.\n\nOpportunity Title: NINDS Renewal Awards of SBIR Phase II Grants (Phase IIB) for Clinical Trials and Clinical Research (R44 Clinical Trial...\n\nOpportunity Title: California Education Learning Lab's AI Challenge Funder/Agency: Governor's Office of Planning and Research (OPR)...\n\nOpportunity Title: Draft Module Announcement; Universal Patching and Remediation for Autonomous Defense (UPGRADE) Funder/Agency:...\n\n",
