    "slug": "cal-oes-physical-and-digital-infrastructure-security-grant-df-program-for-health-care-facilities",
    "title": "Cal OES Physical and Digital Infrastructure Security Grant (DF) Program For Health Care Facilities - Due 06/4/24",
    "excerpt": "Physical and Digital Infrastructure Security Grant (DF) Program For Health Care Facilities RFP Funder/Agency: California Governor's Office of Emergency Services (Cal OES) Opportunity Number: 60510 Des...",
    "bodyText": "\n\nSearch\n\nOpportunity Title:\n\nPhysical and Digital Infrastructure Security Grant (DF) Program For Health Care Facilities RFP\n\n \n\nFunder/Agency:\n\nCalifornia Governor's Office of Emergency Services (Cal OES)\n\n \n\nOpportunity Number:\n\n60510\n\n \n\nDescription:\n\nThe purpose of the DF Program is to provide funding for physical facility and digital security enhancements to health care facilities providing abortion-related services and reproductive health care services throughout California that may be the target of violence and vandalism.\n\n\n\n\nAllowable categories of cost/activities under the DF Program are Planning, Contracted Security Personnel, Cybersecurity, Equipment, Training, and Management and Administration (M&A).\n\n\n\n\nThe 2022-23 California State Budget appropriated $20 million to the Department of Health Care Access and Information (HCAI) “to deliver capital infrastructure support for securing physical and digital infrastructure to facilities providing reproductive health care.” Of those funds, $19 million is available for grants to facilities in California that provide abortion and reproductive health care services. HCAI has contracted with the California Governor’s Office of Emergency Services (Cal OES) to administer the grant program.\n\n \n\nEligibility:\n\nBusiness\n\nNonprofit\n\nTribal Government\n\nOther Legal Entity\n\n \n\nAward Details:\n\nTotal Amount Available:\n\n$7,798,822\n\n\n\n\nMaximum Award:\n\n$750,000\n\n \n\nDeadline:\n\nApplications Due June 04, 2024\n\n \n\nOpportunity Link\n\n \n\nGrant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation.\n\nOpportunity Title: NINDS Renewal Awards of SBIR Phase II Grants (Phase IIB) for Clinical Trials and Clinical Research (R44 Clinical Trial...\n\nOpportunity Title: Draft Module Announcement; Universal Patching and Remediation for Autonomous Defense (UPGRADE) Funder/Agency:...\n\nOpportunity Title: ROSS (Resident Opportunity and Self-Sufficiency) Service Coordinator Program - FY2024 - NOFO Funder/Agency: Department...\n\n",
    "category": "Health"
